A||N||6||fsrowsell||Buying A Car From Canada||||1||
Z||000000||fsrowsell||08-25-2000||07:10 PM||||Anyone here that's from the US, ever bought a car from someone in Canada? I have a guy in Kansas City who want's to buy my car, but he doesn't know what you rules are for buying a car out of Country.... Thanks ||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnsFiero||08-25-2000||09:53 PM||||Based on my limited research on the subject, it looks like the KC buyer would have to deal with customs when bringing the car back to the U.S.  Here is a link that might help.  <A HREF="http://www.customs.ustreas.gov/impoexpo/impoexpo.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.customs.ustreas.gov/impoexpo/impoexpo.htm</A> <P>Good Luck||||reg||1
Z||000002||olympic||08-25-2000||10:08 PM||||Here's another helpful link: <A HREF="http://www.nhtsa.dot.gov/cars/rules/import/can9909.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.nhtsa.dot.gov/cars/rules/import/can9909.htm</A> <P>If the car is more than 3 years old and manufactured in the US or Canada there wont be any duty.  Basically the car just has to meet US safety and emmissions standards and Canadian vehicles should pass that test easily.  Just have the proper documentation(customs agents love lots of documentation) and all should go well.  There may be some fees payable at the border so be prepared for that.<P>   Also, your buyer will probably have to trailer the car home.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fsrowsell||08-25-2000||10:33 PM||||Thanks Guys, I called a Transport Company and they said they would do a door to door move for me for $1530.00US.<BR>That way they would be the one's dealing with customs...||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||08-26-2000||10:53 AM||||YIIIKES!!!! $1500 to move a car? Don't they have Fiero's in Kansas City? It cost me 1/3 of that to have my non-running Fiero shipped from Caliornia to Oklahoma, and there are a boatload more Fieros still in California.  Good luck to you on selling your car out of country, but I can't see what would make a car so unique that I would spend $1500 premium over cost to have it.  This isn't meant as a flame, rather more like a reality check.<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||fsrowsell||08-26-2000||11:28 AM||||This is the car that the gentleman in Kansas City is buying.<BR>V8 Powered Ferrari 328 GTS Replica<BR> <A HREF="http://members.home.net/fsrowsell/mycar.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/fsrowsell/mycar.jpg</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||08-26-2000||01:33 PM||||drewl.... OK, that makes a lot more sense then paying an additional $1500 for a 2M4 with a leaky duke, hehe. Good luck on working out the particulars.  ||||reg||1
